---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Disclosure | Boise Tree Pros"
  description="How Boise Tree Pros works, how calls placed through this site are connected to independent contractors, and how we are compensated."
  canonical="https://boisetreepro.com/disclosure/"
  ogTitle="Disclosure | Boise Tree Pros"
  ogDescription="How Boise Tree Pros works, how calls are connected to independent contractors, and how we are compensated."
  ogImage="https://boisetreepro.com/images/og-image.png"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
<style>
    body { font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif; color: #363636; background: #FAF0E6; }
    h1,h2,h3,h4 { font-family: 'Zilla Slab', Georgia, serif; }

    .nav-link { color: #FAF0E6; text-decoration: none; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 6px; transition: background-color 0.18s, color 0.18s; }
    .nav-link:hover { background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.12); }
    .nav-link:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #87CEEB; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .nav-link:active { opacity: 0.7; }

    .dropdown-link { display: flex; align-items: center; padding: 10px 18px; min-height: 48px; font-size: 14px; color: #363636; text-decoration: none; transition: background-color 0.2s, color 0.2s, opacity 0.2s; outline: none; }
    .dropdown-link:hover { background-color: #f0e8de; color: #1A531A; }
    .dropdown-link:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #1A531A; outline-offset: -2px; }
    .dropdown-link:active { background-color: #e0d4c4; }

    .footer-link { color: #d4c5b0; text-decoration: none; font-size: 14px; transition: color 0.18s; }
    .footer-link:hover { color: #FAF0E6; }
    .footer-link:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #87CEEB; outline-offset: 2px; border-radius: 2px; }
    .footer-link:active { opacity: 0.7; }

    .prose h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1A531A; margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    .prose h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; color: #363636; margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem; }
    .prose p { line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .prose ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .prose ul li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; line-height: 1.7; }
    .prose strong { color: #1a1a1a; font-weight: 600; }
    .prose a { color: #1A531A; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
    .prose a:hover { color: #8B5A2B; }

    .callout { background: #fff; border-left: 4px solid #1A531A; border-radius: 6px; padding: 20px 24px; margin: 0 0 2rem; }
    .callout p { margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; }

    #mobile-menu { display: none; }
    #mobile-menu.open { display: block; }
  </style>
<script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://boisetreepro.com/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Disclosure", "item": "https://boisetreepro.com/disclosure/" }
    ]
  }
  </script>
  </Fragment>

<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-4">
  <ol style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:flex;gap:8px;font-size:13px;color:#888;">
    <li><a href="/" style="color:#8B5A2B;text-decoration:none;">Home</a></li>
    <li>/</li>
    <li style="color:#363636;">Disclosure</li>
  </ol>
</nav>

<section style="background:linear-gradient(135deg, #0F3010 0%, #1A531A 40%, #2A6B2A 100%);padding:64px 0 72px;">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div style="max-width:720px;">
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,44px);font-weight:700;color:#FAF0E6;line-height:1.15;margin-bottom:16px;letter-spacing:-0.02em;">Disclosure</h1>
      <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:rgba(250,240,230,0.85);max-width:620px;">How this site works, who actually shows up at your property, and how we get paid. In plain terms.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="padding:64px 0 80px;">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="prose" style="max-width:760px;">

      <div class="callout">
        <p><strong>The short version:</strong> Boise Tree Pros is a referral service, not a tree care contractor. We do not own trucks, employ crews, or perform tree work. When you call the number on this site, you are connected to an independent tree care company that serves your area, and we may be paid for making that connection.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <p>We publish information about tree care in Boise and the Treasure Valley — what work costs, what the local code requires, which species struggle in our alkaline soil, and how to tell a genuine hazard from a tree that just looks bad. The goal is that you arrive at a decision better informed than you were.</p>
      <p>When you are ready to get the work done, we connect you by phone with an independent tree care contractor serving your area.</p>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not perform tree removal, trimming, stump grinding, or any other tree work.</li>
        <li>We do not employ arborists, climbers, or ground crews.</li>
        <li>We do not own or operate equipment.</li>
        <li>We do not set the price you are quoted, and we are not party to your agreement with the contractor.</li>
        <li>We do not supervise, inspect, or guarantee the work performed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we are compensated</h2>
      <p>We are paid for connecting you with a contractor. That payment comes from the contractor or from an advertising network acting on their behalf, and it is not added to your bill. You pay the contractor directly for the work at whatever price the two of you agree.</p>
      <p>We think it is fair for you to know this before you pick up the phone, which is why it appears in the footer of every page on this site rather than only here.</p>

      <h2>Credentials, licensing, and insurance</h2>
      <p>Any statement on this site about certification, licensing, or insurance describes the standards we expect of the contractors we work with. It is not a warranty about the specific company that takes your job, because we are not that company.</p>
      <p><strong>Verify credentials yourself before work begins.</strong> This matters more in tree work than in most trades, because an uninsured climber injured on your property can become your financial problem. Specifically:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Ask for a certificate of general liability insurance sent to you directly by the insurer, not a copy handed over by the contractor.</li>
        <li>Confirm workers' compensation coverage for everyone who will be on your property.</li>
        <li>If an ISA-certified arborist is important to your job, ask for that individual's name and verify it in the <a href="https://www.isa-arbor.com/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">International Society of Arboriculture</a> directory. Certification belongs to people, not companies.</li>
        <li>Get the scope, the cleanup, and the stump in writing before work starts.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Our guide to <a href="/blog/how-to-hire-tree-service-boise/">hiring a tree service in Boise</a> covers this in more detail, and it applies equally to a contractor you reach through this site.</p>

      <h2>Pricing information on this site</h2>
      <p>Every price range published here is a general ballpark for the Boise area, gathered to help you budget and to help you recognise a quote that is unusually high or suspiciously low. Ranges are never a quote, an offer, or a commitment. Only the contractor who inspects your property can price your job, and that number governs.</p>

      <h2>Availability and response times</h2>
      <p>Availability, hours, and how quickly someone can reach you depend on the contractor who receives your call and on conditions at the time. After a major windstorm, every tree company in the valley is busy at once. We cannot guarantee a response time.</p>

      <h2>Emergencies</h2>
      <p>If a tree or limb has fallen on a structure, a vehicle, or a person, or if anything is touching a power line, call 911 and your utility first. Do not wait on a contractor, and do not approach a downed line. Idaho Power handles vegetation contacting distribution lines.</p>

      <h2>Content on this site</h2>
      <p>Articles here are general information about tree care, local regulations, and property issues in Idaho. They are not legal advice, engineering advice, or a substitute for a qualified arborist inspecting your specific tree. Codes change and enforcement varies between Boise, Meridian, Nampa, Caldwell, Eagle, and Garden City — confirm anything consequential with the relevant city before acting on it.</p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>If anything here is unclear, or you want to know how a particular call was handled, <a href="/#contact">get in touch</a>.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:2.5rem;font-size:14px;color:#888;">Last updated: 19 August 2026</p>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
